# Document Purpose

This document serves as the official Functional Architecture and Technical Specification for the Ravion DPR system.

Its purpose is to define the business requirements, software architecture, module relationships, workflows, database structure, implementation strategy, and future roadmap for the Ravion DPR platform.

This document is intended to remain the primary reference throughout the lifecycle of the application and should be updated whenever new modules or architectural changes are introduced.

---

# Intended Audience

This document is designed for:

* Product Owners
* Project Managers
* Software Architects
* Laravel Developers
* UI/UX Designers
* QA Engineers
* Implementation Engineers
* Future Development Teams
* System Administrators

---

# Project Overview

Ravion DPR is an enterprise-level Construction Daily Progress Reporting and Project Management platform designed specifically for residential, commercial, and industrial construction projects.

The application is intended to digitize all site-level activities while providing complete visibility to management through structured workflows, standardized master data, approvals, dashboards, reports, and inventory management.

Unlike a simple DPR application, Ravion DPR is being architected as a scalable Construction ERP capable of supporting multiple companies, multiple projects, multiple users, and future enterprise modules such as Procurement, Inventory, BOQ, QA/QC, Safety, Equipment, Billing, CRM, and Odoo Integration.

---

# Vision Statement

To build a modern, scalable, and intelligent Construction ERP that enables engineers, project managers, contractors, management, and stakeholders to collaborate through a unified digital platform while maintaining complete transparency, accountability, and operational efficiency.

---

# Mission

The mission of Ravion DPR is to eliminate manual reporting, disconnected spreadsheets, paper-based approvals, and fragmented project information by providing a centralized ERP platform for construction project execution.

The platform aims to become the single source of truth for project progress, labour deployment, material movement, planning, approvals, reporting, and management decision-making.

---

# Core Objectives

The primary objectives of Ravion DPR are:

* Digitize Daily Progress Reporting
* Standardize all construction master data
* Improve project monitoring
* Increase reporting accuracy
* Provide real-time management visibility
* Reduce manual paperwork
* Strengthen auditability
* Improve material accountability
* Enable workflow-based approvals
* Build a scalable ERP foundation

---

# Business Goals

The application has been designed to achieve the following business outcomes:

## Engineering

* Faster DPR preparation
* Reduced repetitive data entry
* Standardized reporting
* Mobile-friendly operation
* Accurate labour reporting
* Accurate material reporting

---

## Project Management

* Daily project visibility
* Labour productivity tracking
* Material monitoring
* Delay identification
* Work progress analysis
* Better planning

---

## PMO

* Centralized DPR review
* Standardized approval process
* Quality verification
* Progress validation
* Cross-project monitoring

---

## Management

* Executive dashboards
* Multi-project monitoring
* KPI reporting
* Resource utilization
* Decision support
* Historical analytics

---

# Design Philosophy

The application follows the following guiding principles.

## Simplicity

Every screen should require minimal training and allow engineers to complete daily reporting quickly.

---

## Standardization

Master data shall be maintained centrally to eliminate inconsistent naming and duplicate records.

---

## Traceability

Every transaction must be traceable through complete audit logs.

---

## Scalability

The architecture shall support future ERP modules without major redesign.

---

## Security

Role-based permissions shall ensure users only access information relevant to their responsibilities.

---

## Performance

The application shall remain responsive even with large datasets, multiple concurrent users, and multiple active projects.

---

## Maintainability

The software shall follow modular architecture, Laravel best practices, reusable components, and clean coding standards to simplify long-term maintenance.

---

