# Chapter 3 – User Roles, Permissions & Security Architecture

---

# Introduction

The Ravion DPR platform follows a **Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)** architecture.

Every authenticated user is assigned one or more predefined roles. Permissions are granted to roles rather than individual users, ensuring centralized administration, simplified maintenance, and improved security.

The RBAC model ensures that users can only access the data and functionality required to perform their assigned responsibilities.

---

# Security Objectives

The security model has been designed to achieve the following objectives:

* Protect sensitive project information.
* Prevent unauthorized data access.
* Restrict approval authority.
* Maintain complete auditability.
* Simplify user administration.
* Support future enterprise modules.

---

# User Hierarchy

The application follows the organizational hierarchy shown below.

```text
Management
        │
Administrator
        │
DGM
        │
PMO
        │
Project Manager (Future)
        │
Site Engineer
        │
Store Incharge (Future)
        │
Supervisor (Future)
        │
Contractor (Future Portal)
```

Each level inherits greater operational responsibility but not unrestricted system access.

---

# Standard User Roles

The following roles are currently defined.

## Administrator

### Purpose

Complete system administration.

### Responsibilities

* Manage users
* Manage roles
* Manage permissions
* Configure masters
* View all projects
* Approve where required
* Audit monitoring
* System maintenance

### Access

✔ Complete application

---

## DGM (Deputy General Manager)

### Purpose

Corporate-level project monitoring.

### Responsibilities

* Monitor all projects
* Review dashboards
* View reports
* Review DPRs
* Approve selected workflows
* Performance monitoring

### Access

* All projects
* Reports
* Dashboards
* PMO functions

---

## PMO (Project Management Office)

### Purpose

Central technical verification.

### Responsibilities

* Review DPR submissions
* Verify labour
* Verify materials
* Approve DPR
* Reject DPR
* Enter review remarks
* Project monitoring

### Access

* PMO Queue
* DPR Review
* Reports

Cannot:

* Delete master data
* Modify user permissions
* System configuration

---

## Site Engineer

### Purpose

Daily project execution and reporting.

### Responsibilities

* Create DPR
* Edit Draft DPR
* Submit DPR
* Record labour
* Record material received
* Record material consumption
* Record material requirement
* Update project progress

Cannot:

* Approve DPR
* Edit approved DPR
* Access system settings

---

