# Permission Matrix

| Module            | Admin |  DGM |   PMO   |    Engineer   |
| ----------------- | :---: | :--: | :-----: | :-----------: |
| Dashboard         |   ✔   |   ✔  |    ✔    |       ✔       |
| Projects          |   ✔   | View |   View  | Assigned Only |
| DPR Create        |   ✔   | View |   View  |       ✔       |
| DPR Submit        |   ✔   | View |   View  |       ✔       |
| DPR Approve       |   ✔   |   ✔  |    ✔    |       ✖       |
| Labour Reports    |   ✔   |   ✔  |    ✔    |       ✔       |
| Material Received |   ✔   |   ✔  |    ✔    |       ✔       |
| Material Consumed |   ✔   |   ✔  |    ✔    |       ✔       |
| Masters           |   ✔   | View | Limited |       ✖       |
| Audit Logs        |   ✔   |   ✔  |   View  |       ✖       |

---

# Project-Level Security

Engineers should only access projects assigned to them.

Rules:

* Assigned Engineer → Assigned Projects
* PMO → All Projects
* DGM → All Projects
* Administrator → Complete Access

This rule is already implemented for project selection and should remain consistent throughout the application.

---

# Approval Authority

Only authorized roles may approve business transactions.

Examples:

| Transaction           | Approval Authority |
| --------------------- | ------------------ |
| DPR                   | PMO / Admin / DGM  |
| Material Verification | PMO                |
| Future Purchase Order | Purchase Manager   |
| Future Payment        | Accounts           |

---

# Audit Security

Every sensitive operation shall generate an audit record.

Tracked actions include:

* Create
* Update
* Delete (where permitted)
* Submit
* Approve
* Reject
* Activate
* Deactivate

Future enhancements:

* Login History
* Failed Login Attempts
* Session Tracking
* IP Address Logging
* Browser Information

---

# Future Security Enhancements

The following enterprise-grade security features are planned:

* Two-Factor Authentication (2FA)
* Password Expiry Policies
* Account Lockout
* Single Sign-On (SSO)
* LDAP / Active Directory Integration
* API Token Authentication
* Device Recognition
* Session Timeout
* Security Notifications

